  "format": "boys.path-declarations/1",
  "why": "One declaration per body that evaluates a Boys value for a caller. One arithmetic - a seed and an upward recurrence in a named division form - is written out once per lane, per shape and per fit route, and nothing enforced that the copies stayed a family: one body was corrected while thirteen siblings kept the arithmetic it was corrected from, and every one of them passed its published bound, because every bound this library publishes is ABSOLUTE and an absolute bound at large argument is vacuous. What went unseen was that the bodies were never LISTED. This table is the list. It states, per body, the bar that body is held to and the site that holds it there; tools/check_paths_declared.py reads the bodies out of the source, joins them against this table in both directions, and refuses a body that is not here. A body added to the library fails the check until a row is added for it, and a row whose body has been removed fails until the row goes.",
